# `docs/oracle/NOW.md` — the shared session

Cursor Cloud, Cursor Desktop and Claude Code all work this repo. **They cannot see each
other's chats.** There is no shared conversation and no Claude MCP in Cursor. The only
things all of them read are **HubSpot** and **`docs/oracle/NOW.md`**.

NOW.md is not documentation. It is the working memory of whichever agent is not
currently running. Write it as a handover note to a colleague who starts blind.

## Rules

1. **Read it first**, before any work, every session — **PART 1 is the protocol, follow
   it.** It says what is in flight, whose move each item is, and what is known broken.
2. **Claim before you touch.** Add your row to the session board in PART 1 and push it
   *before* editing shared code or restarting a service. Delete the row when you stop.
   A claim older than 2h with no newer commit is dead — take it.
3. **🚨 Push it to `main`. Always. Even when your work is on a branch.**
4. **Never destroy:** no `--force`, never `reset`/`checkout --` a file you did not write
   this session, never blind `git pull` on Oracle's `cto-aipa`. Same file both changed →
   merge, do not overwrite; the version carrying a verification wins.
5. **Catch the other's fall.** Run the five-item start-of-session check in PART 1 §4.
   Every item on it is a failure that actually shipped — especially §4.3: confirm the last
   change produced **output**, not just that it ran.
6. **Check §6 DELIBERATE before "fixing" anything that looks broken.** Wellfound returning
   zero, YC not being scraped, Oracle's checkout lagging and the failing Claude eval are
   all intentional, and each has cost someone an investigation already.
7. **A work product lives in a file or in HubSpot — never only in a chat.** Earned 1 Sep
   2026: preparation for a role was drafted in a Cursor chat and existed nowhere else. Every
   Cursor database on the laptop was searched — global storage plus all ten workspace stores,
   every table and column — **zero hits**. Unrecoverable, and the other agent would have
   rewritten it from nothing. A letter, brief, application answer, plan or set of findings
   goes to a committed file in `docs/` or a HubSpot note on the deal, immediately. Chat is
   where work is discussed, not where it is kept.
8. **Pause with a handoff block** — DONE / NEXT / VERIFIED BY / RISK. An agent that stops
   without one has lost the work even if the code is committed.
9. **Keep it to one screen per part.** It is a queue, not a history. Delete finished
   lines; git log keeps the record.

## Why rule 3 is in capitals

**Earned 30 Aug 2026.** NOW.md was created on 25 Aug on branch
`cursor/intelliops-bd-money-play-abc0` and never merged. From `main` — which is what
Claude Code reads and what Oracle runs — the file did not exist, so a second version was
written from scratch five days later. Both agents were correct about their own branch and
neither could see the other. Nothing was lost, but the coordination file had failed
silently at its only job for five days.

**A shared-state file on a branch the other tool never reads is a private note.**

If the work must live on a branch, send the NOW.md update to `main` on its own, and say
there that the branch exists and what is on it. Never leave the handover note inside the
thing being handed over.

## What goes in it

- The money queue: what is in flight and **whose move it is** (Elena's vs the agent's)
- Anything **open or known-broken** a new session must not assume works
- Anything **stranded on a branch**, plus a warning if merging would delete work
- Standing traps that keep costing time
- What just landed, briefly, so nobody re-investigates a solved problem

**Not** in it: architecture, post-mortems, or anything already in `docs/`, the memory
files or the AI Ops Wiki. Link to those instead.

> The same contract is in `CLAUDE.md` for Claude Code. If you change one, change both —
> a rule that only one side can read is the bug this rule exists to prevent.
